1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,481
The disagreement was about one week: ship on Friday, or wait beyond the weekend and lose the holiday slot.

2
00:00:07,481 --> 00:00:11,547
“We are always doing this,” Maya said.

3
00:00:11,547 --> 00:00:23,717
“We spend Monday to Thursday arguing and then hurry on Friday.” The police had asked for a signed guideline; the inspector had asked for two more days.

4
00:00:23,717 --> 00:00:28,862
“Certainly the worst option is a dash at dawn,” she said.

5
00:00:28,862 --> 00:00:33,502
“And the catch is that we have already promised.”

6
00:00:33,502 --> 00:00:36,687
Lin argued for a speedy release.

7
00:00:36,687 --> 00:00:46,517
A successful release would be a Christmas present for the council; a delayed one would cost the acquisition and lose the festival coverage.

8
00:00:46,517 --> 00:00:51,097
“The era of the perfect launch is over,” he said.

9
00:00:51,097 --> 00:00:57,192
“The customary thing is to go out on Monday and fix it on Tuesday.”

10
00:00:57,192 --> 00:01:00,608
Maya argued for a durable release.

11
00:01:00,608 --> 00:01:06,238
“Wednesday is the only weekday the inspector can come,” she said.

12
00:01:06,238 --> 00:01:11,593
“Thursday is the marathon; Saturday is the day we sleep.

13
00:01:11,593 --> 00:01:24,293
A pregnancy of nine months does not become negotiable because Thanksgiving arrives.” The prohibitive cost of a recall was the part he kept overlooking.

14
00:01:24,293 --> 00:01:36,873
Amid the argument, the coordinator produced the sequential figures: the accumulative risk of the last three releases, measured evenly across the weekend and the weekday.

15
00:01:36,873 --> 00:01:41,853
“Two successive releases went out overnight,” she said.

16
00:01:41,853 --> 00:01:46,118
“The excellence of the first hid the failure of the second.

17
00:01:46,118 --> 00:01:51,033
In the meantime, nobody ran the test.”

18
00:01:51,033 --> 00:02:03,353
The compromise was expensive and honest: release on Friday for the festival, and hasten the inspection so that the new guideline could be established by the following week.

19
00:02:03,353 --> 00:02:09,198
“The usual guideline is written for the best case,” the inspector said.

20
00:02:09,198 --> 00:02:20,598
“Write the other one.” They listened to each other for the first time that day, and the cost of the argument was one weekend of running repairs.

21
00:02:20,598 --> 00:02:29,288
For the council, the cost was one more day in court; for the team, it was a new line in the guideline.

22
00:02:29,288 --> 00:02:35,933
“Certainly the catch is that we must go back and establish who pays,” Maya said.

23
00:02:35,933 --> 00:02:51,721
“If we do not listen to the other side, the help we give will be a move in the wrong direction.” They put their hearts into the last paragraph, and the inspector, in the end, signed it.
